{% doc %}
  blocks/faq-row.liquid

  One question and whatever answers it, inside a `<faq-accordion>`.

  ## The answer is blocks, not a rich text field

  It used to be one `richtext` setting, which meant an answer could only ever be
  prose. Half the questions a store actually gets are answered better by
  something else — a size table, a delivery banner, an image of the returns
  label, a button to the policy page — and none of that fits in a rich text
  field.

  So the panel is `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` and the row accepts `@theme`:
  every block the theme has is available inside an answer, and the Text block is
  what the preset puts there, so the default row is still a question and a
  paragraph. Nothing here knows what a Text block is.

  ## Still a `<details>`


  Same reasoning as `blocks/collapsible.liquid`: the disclosure is native, so the
  answer is on the page with JavaScript off, `<summary>` is already a button with
  an expanded state to a screen reader, and the browser's own in-page search
  finds the text. Nothing here re-implements that with a `<button>` and an
  `aria-expanded` of its own.

  The open and close motion belongs to `<accordion-element>` in
  `assets/modules.js` — a measured WAAPI height animation that every other
  disclosure group in the theme already uses. This file contributes markup, not a
  second animation system: the panel is a plain wrapper precisely so that
  animation has a single box to measure.

  ## Two icons in one summary, and only one of them means "open"

  The toggle is `snippets/icon.liquid` like everything else — a **plus** whose
  upright bar travels onto the crossbar and stops there as a minus, or a
  **chevron** that turns. It used to be two pseudo-elements crossed in CSS,
  which is the same glyph drawn a second time in a second place.

  The icon beside the question is content, and it does not move at all. That is
  worth stating because it did: the group rule in `assets/base.css` rotated
  every `.icon` inside an open summary, so a truck or a padlock a merchant had
  chosen turned upside down along with the marker. The rule names the chevron
  and the plus now.

  ## The icon is the Subheading block's, by reference

  `blocks/subheading.liquid` settled how an icon is chosen in this theme —
  **None**, **Icon** or **Image**, one field per source, the chosen one shown and
  the others hidden — and the same four setting ids are used here (`icon_source`,
  `icon`, `icon_image`, `icon_image_alt`) so a merchant who has configured a
  Subheading already knows this control. The glyph comes from
  `snippets/icon.liquid` and an upload from `snippets/image.liquid`, which is
  where every other icon and image in the theme comes from.

  Only the box is this file's own, and it is derived rather than configured: the
  merchant sets **Icon size** and the tile around it follows, so the two can
  never disagree.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign question = s.question
  assign icon_source = s.icon_source | default: 'none'
  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  assign has_icon = false
  if icon_source == 'icon' and s.icon != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif
  if icon_source == 'image' and s.icon_image != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  assign toggle = s.toggle_style | default: 'plus'

  # The icon tile grows with the glyph rather than taking a second slider that
  # can be set smaller than the thing it contains.
  assign icon_box = icon_size | plus: 12
-%}

{%- if question != blank -%}
  {%- capture row_style -%}
    {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
    {%- if has_icon -%}
      --faq-row-icon-size: {{ icon_size }}px;
      --faq-row-icon-box: {{ icon_box }}px;
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <details
    class="faq-row faq-row--toggle-{{ toggle }}{% if has_icon %} faq-row--has-icon{% endif %}"
    {% if s.open_by_default %}open data-default-open{% endif %}
    data-block-spacing
    style="{{ row_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <summary class="faq-row__summary">
      {%- if has_icon -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No `aria-hidden` on the tile. `snippets/icon.liquid` already hides the
          glyphs it renders, and an upload carries its own **Alt text** field —
          hiding the wrapper would silently discard whatever the merchant typed
          into it. Each source keeps its own semantics, as in the Subheading
          block.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="faq-row__icon">
          {%- if icon_source == 'image' -%}
            {% render 'image',
               image: s.icon_image,
               alt: s.icon_image_alt,
               sizes: '48px',
               wrapper_class: 'faq-row__icon-image' %}
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <span class="faq-row__question">{{ question }}</span>

      {%- comment -%}
        Decorative. `<summary>` conveys the expanded state already, so labelling
        this would announce the same thing twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="faq-row__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if toggle == 'arrow' -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 14, class: 'faq-row__chevron' %}
        {%- else -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'plus', size: 14, class: 'faq-row__plus' %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </summary>

    {%- comment -%}
      A plain wrapper, deliberately. `<accordion-element>` animates the height of
      the `<details>` itself and measures this box to find the end value; a
      `grid-template-rows` trick here would animate against that measurement and
      land with a visible jump.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="faq-row__panel">
      <div class="faq-row__answer">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.faq_row.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@theme" },
    { "type": "@app" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "label": "t:blocks.faq_row.settings.question.label",
      "default": "How long does delivery take?"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "open_by_default",
      "label": "t:blocks.faq_row.settings.open_by_default.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.faq_row.settings.open_by_default.info",
      "default": false
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.subheading.headers.icon" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.faq_row.paragraphs.icon" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_source",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.none.label" },
        { "value": "icon", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "image", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "icon"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "star", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "check", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "heart", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "truck", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "refresh", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "lock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__7.label" },
        { "value": "clock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__8.label" },
        { "value": "location", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__9.label" },
        { "value": "mail", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__10.label" },
        { "value": "note", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__11.label" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__12.label" }
      ],
      "default": "note",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'icon' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "icon_image",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "icon_image_alt",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_size.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.faq_row.settings.icon_size.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "extra_small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "extra_large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__6.label" }
      ],
      "default": "medium",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_size_custom",
      "label": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.label",
      "info": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.info",
      "min": 12,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' and block.settings.icon_size == 'custom' }}"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.collapsible.headers.toggle" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "toggle_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.collapsible.settings.toggle_style.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "plus", "label": "t:blocks.collapsible.settings.toggle_style.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "arrow", "label": "t:blocks.collapsible.settings.toggle_style.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "plus"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.faq_row.name",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Orders ship within two working days. You will get a tracking link as soon as the parcel leaves us.</p>",
            "preset": "paragraph"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
